---
description: ML/AI pipeline rules for data prep, training, evaluation, and serving
version: 1.5.0
globs: [
  "ml/**",
  "ai/**",
  "models/**",
  "training/**",
  "apps/**/ml/**",
  "apps/**/ai/**",
  "packages/**/ml/**",
  "packages/**/ai/**",
  "**/*.ipynb"
]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Track datasets and model artifacts with lineage and versioning; record training configs and seeds.
- Separate train/val/test; prevent leakage and ensure reproducibility with deterministic steps.
- Monitor data drift and model performance post-deploy; alert on significant drops.
- Validate inputs/outputs at service boundaries; cap payload sizes and enforce schemas.
- Prefer idempotent, resumable pipelines; checkpoint long runs and clean up temp artifacts.
- Document evaluation metrics and acceptance thresholds; include fairness/bias checks where relevant.
- Publish model cards for shipped models (intended use, metrics, limits) and record safety/abuse evals.
- Scrub prompts/responses of PII/secrets; apply allow/deny filters and logging with redaction.
- Secure model endpoints: authZ, rate limits, request/response logging without sensitive payloads.
- Optimize serving for latency and cost; batch where possible and set resource limits.
